{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall come.</b> And you shall not see any of these." "<b>To your fathers.</b> His father was an idolater, and he informs him that he will come to him? This teaches you that Terach repented." "<b>You shall be buried in a good old age.</b> That Ishmael will repent in his days, and Esau will not go forth into evil ways in his days; and therefore he died five years before his time, and on that very day Esau rebelled."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "Rashi writes ה' (five) as an abbreviated numeral; resolved as five years, per Genesis 25:7 (Abraham lived 175) and 25:26 (Isaac was 60 at the birth of Esau), giving Esau's age 15 at Abraham's death, i.e., five years before the age of legal majority (20)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:48.814302339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}